    "text": "96\n\n The Problem with \u201cPassive Income\u201d Plumbing Companies\nHi Sara,\nIf you\u2019ve been on YouTube in the last six months, you\u2019ve probably seen it: another glossy video telling you that buying a \u201cboring\u201d business (think HVAC, plumbing, car washes) is your ticket to sipping champagne on a yacht while your new company runs itself.\nLet\u2019s burst that bubble\u2014gently, but thoroughly. Spoiler alert: there\u2019s nothing \u201cpassive\u201d about clogged toilets and broken soap dispensers.\nHere\u2019s the Not-So-Boring Truth:\nThese businesses aren\u2019t bad buys\u2014in fact, they can be excellent ones\u2014but they are people-heavy, compliance-laden, and deeply operational.\nYou want to run a car wash? Fantastic. Just know that someone\u2019s going to have to restock soap, clean up after messy customers, and handle complaints from people convinced your very expensive machinery scratched their 2002 Honda Civic.\nYou want to buy an HVAC business with zero experience in HVAC? I love your optimism. But unless you\u2019re a professional management company with a team ready to run the business for you, prepare for a crash course in employee drama, regulatory headaches, and insurance chaos.\nHere\u2019s Why People Sell These \u201cCash Cows\u201d:\nBecause they\u2019re tired. Because they\u2019ve been in the trenches dealing with payroll, collections, broken equipment, and burnt-out technicians. Buying one of these businesses isn\u2019t a walk in the park\u2014it\u2019s a full sprint through a people-powered obstacle course.\nSo, Should You Buy One?\nMaybe! If you\u2019ve got the grit, the systems, and the support, it can be a profitable ride.\nBut here\u2019s an insider tip: accounting practices are flying under the radar right now. \n\nThey\u2019ve got:\nGreat margins (sometimes 30-40%!)\n\nClean books (literally their job)\n\nLess red tape (particularly if you\u2019re buying a non-attest firm)\n\nWe\u2019ve got more on this at Deal Academy, where we walk you through how to spot the right opportunities and avoid the common pitfalls that turn dream deals into disasters.\nWant to learn how to buy a business without buying a headache?\nCheck out our courses and stay tuned\u2014we\u2019re doing a deep dive soon on how to evaluate and acquire accounting firms the smart way.\n\nTo actually boring (and profitable) businesses,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
